 ok←run _on_Select message;object;pgs;sel;waspage;newpage;wasndx;newndx;by
 ⍝ Intercept an activation of a Page's TabButton and do any preliminary checking/work on the Page as a whole unit

 object←⊃message ⍝ The Page's TabButton that was pressed
 :If 'SubForm'≡object ##.##.∆WG'Type' ⋄ ok←1 ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Ignore Select events coming directly from the SubForm instead of the TabButton
 by←3⊃message,2 ⍝ Assume the mouse changed it (if we're not told from another routine) ⍝? Can we detect a keyboard-invoked Select here?
 newpage←object ##.##.∆WG'TabObj' ⍝ The matching Page (SubForm) object
 sel←⊃newpage._Ancestry ⍝ The Selector (parent) object
 waspage←(sel ##.##.∆WG'TabObj')##.##.∆WG'TabObj' ⍝ The previously-selected Page (SubForm) object that we're about to leave
 pgs←sel sel._Class.pages ⍬ ⍝ What are our sibling Page (object) names (in order)?
 (wasndx newndx)←(1+≢pgs)|pgs⍳##.##.LeafName¨⍕¨waspage newpage
 :If ok←wasndx=newndx ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ If the page hasn't actually changed, don't do anything
 :If ok←~(⊂'Validate'##.##.Event waspage ##.##.Application by(newndx,wasndx))∊⍬ 1⍴¨0 ⍝ Validate previous Page
 :AndIf ok←~(⊂'Validate'##.##.Event sel ##.##.Application by(newndx,wasndx))∊⍬ 1⍴¨0 ⍝ Validate Selector
     waspage._visible←0 ⋄ newpage._visible←1 ⍝ Manage the _visible properties ourselves!
     ok←1⊣'Change'##.##.Event sel ##.##.Application newndx wasndx ⍝ A successful Selector Change is occurring
 :EndIf
